DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The tthhrr__sseellff() system call stores the system-wide thread identifier for
     the current kernel-scheduled thread in the variable pointed by the argu‐
     ment _i_d.

     The thread identifier is an integer in the range from PID_MAX + 2
     (100001) to INT_MAX.  The thread identifier is guaranteed to be unique at
     any given time, for each running thread in the system.  After the thread
     exits, the identifier may be reused.

